---
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<section class="section about" id="about">
  <div class="container grid">
    <div class="left reveal">
      <h2>Who I am,<br /><span class="soft">and what I am looking for.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="right reveal" data-delay="1">
      <p class="big">
        I'm {site.name}, a frontend engineer in {site.location}. I founded
        <a href={site.company.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{site.company.name}</a>, a live gift-card and crypto
        to naira exchange with a web app, operator console and Flutter app, and I take on contract builds like the
        <a href="/projects/bethadel-media/">Bethadel Media site</a>. I am looking for a full-time role.
      </p>
      <p>
        What I want: a team that ships to real users, reviews code properly, and lets an engineer own a feature from
        the ticket to production. Frontend-leaning is ideal, full-stack is fine. Remote across EMEA works; so does Lagos or Abuja.
        Running my own product taught me what it costs when something breaks, which is why I test.
      </p>
      <p>
        How I got here: the ALX software engineering programme, which starts in C and Linux, then freelance React work
        for clients, then Payroid. The systems background is the reason my latest project has a README that explains
        its redirect strategy instead of a list of features.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you want to see how I think before you book a call, read the
        <a href="/projects/linkbolt/">LinkBolt case study</a>. It is the closest thing to a work sample I can show
        without a client's permission.
      </p>
      <dl class="facts">
        <div><dt>Based in</dt><dd>{site.location}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>Available now</dd></div> <!-- TODO: add notice period, e.g. "2 weeks notice" -->
        <div><dt>Looking for</dt><dd>Frontend / full-stack · remote (EMEA) or Nigeria</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Education</dt><dd>University of Benin · ALX SE</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.3fr; gap: 3rem; }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3.6rem); position: sticky; top: 6rem; }
  .soft { color: var(--dim); }
  .right { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .big { font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.5rem); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.4; font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .big a { border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); }
  .right p a:not(.big a) { color: var(--text); }
  .facts { margin: 1rem 0 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 1rem; }
  .facts div { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 0.75rem; }
  dt { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--dim); }
  dd { margin: 0.2rem 0 0; color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; } h2 { position: static; } }
</style>
